<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ilham Aliyev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1961</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ilham Aliyev is the president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heydar-aliyev">Heydar Aliyev</a> in 2003. His government has used oil and gas revenue to build up the state and armed forces while suppressing opposition. In 2020 and 2023 Azerbaijan recaptured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagorno-karabakh">Nagorno-Karabakh</a> and the surrounding districts from Armenian forces.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ilham-aliyev.jpg" alt="Ilham Aliyev" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Press Service of the President of the Republic of Azerbaijan · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ilham_Aliyev,_December_2025_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
